I have enough to conclude. Search is the only service whose own resources changed materially. Its CPU rose from about 0.007 to about 2.75 cores in a single pod, while node utilisation stayed low. Its own spans and the user-facing spans that call it stayed near normal, so the propagation to users is weak but present. I'm writing the answer now.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "container_cpu_saturated",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name, round(avg(value),3) AS avg_cpu_cores, round(max(value),3) AS max_cpu_cores FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='container.cpu.usage' AND service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Search pod container CPU usage averages about 2.7 cores during the incident, pinned near a constant ceiling."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name, round(avg(value),4) AS avg_cpu_cores FROM normal_metrics WHERE metric='container.cpu.usage' AND service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Same search pod normally uses about 0.007 cores of CPU, so the increase is roughly 400x."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, round(avg(value),2) AS abn_avg, round(max(value),2) AS abn_max FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric='container.cpu.time' AND service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Search cumulative container CPU time rises sharply in the incident, with peak well above its normal maximum."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, count(*) AS restart_series, max(value) AS max_restarts FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Restart counters show no new restarts, so the search fault is saturation rather than a pod restart."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [
       {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, span_name, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Search.Search/Nearby server spans and frontend client spans to it both appear in the incident window, with the frontend caller seeing the same call."},
       {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT p, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) AS p95_ms, count(*) AS n FROM (SELECT 'abn' p, duration, span_name, attr_span_kind FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', duration, span_name, attr_span_kind FROM normal_traces) WHERE span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Frontend's client-side latency for search stays near normal, so the CPU saturation has little measurable effect on users."}
     ]}
  ]
}
